project Critical Path Autonomy
id critical-path-autonomy
channel #proj-agent-orchestration
canonical_repo evanbrown3000/codex-backend-sdk
source_plan /home/evan/Documents/COLLECTED-BY-EVAN/2026/10/8/critical_path_plan.md
status active

principles
  - The single Cloudflare D1 prompt queue owns priority, leases, dependencies, and completion.
  - The hosted historical rhythm owns ChatGPT chat-mode prompt timing; no scheduled tasks or Work mode.
  - Codex research and external-effect phases must use installed Codex with named employees.
  - No provider terminal reply or source-only commit counts as completion of a TaskFlow step.
  - Agent conversations and files must be centrally ingested and read back without provider re-poll.
  - Keep prompt cost and Codex quota bounded; do not spam ChatGPT.
  - Preserve the source plan and this plan as instruction; do not ask an agent to write a prompt for another agent.

[ ] CP-4-6 deploy and verify an unattended TaskFlow phase controller
    owner: Elliot Mercer
    source: critical_path_plan.md steps 4, 5, and 6
    do:
      - reconcile the returned ChatGPT native-sandbox TaskFlow controller ZIP with current SDK and Cloudflare D1 code
      - run one named Codex research phase that produces a ZIP with a complete hash manifest
      - clock one physical-ZIP ChatGPT chat-mode xhigh turn and centrally read back its terminal report and single work ZIP
      - use another named installed Codex employee to apply the ZIP's EXTERNAL_EFFECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md to the real SDK and Cloudflare runtime
      - install and start the bounded TaskFlow recurrence service on EvanPC
    effect_probe_command: /usr/bin/systemctl --user is-active cognilode-taskflow-phase-controller.service
    effect_probe_expected: active
    done_when:
      - the controller service is active and an unattended recurrence logs a completed external-effect D1 job with a real deployment or service-change identity and central readback
      - the completed ChatGPT phase by itself never releases the dependent step

[ ] CP-7 multi-device home-network failover and sustained recurrence
    depends_on: CP-4-6
    owner: Nadia Brooks
    source: critical_path_plan.md step 7
    do:
      - install the chat-mode actuator on a second eligible home or mobile device and register independent heartbeats
      - verify hosted Cloudflare control and historical rhythm continue while EvanPC is offline
      - exercise real failover and central readback for a clocked chat-mode turn
    done_when:
      - one real provider turn is automatically sent from the alternate device while EvanPC is unavailable and its work ZIP is centrally recovered
